Our changes
-----------
- 2026-10-15: standalone repository created (not a GitHub fork relationship) from the full PCSX2
  history at v2.8.2; branch gt4gs/main.
- 2026-10-15: gt4gs/ documentation (README, BUILD, NOTICE).
- 2026-10-15: .github/workflows/gt4gs-windows.yml, scripts/windows/package-gt4gs.ps1 and the trimmed
  dependency script build-dependencies-gt4gs.bat (upstream's build-dependencies.bat without the Qt
  block; Qt is not needed when ENABLE_QT_UI=OFF).
- 2026-10-15: upstream workflows changed to workflow_dispatch only (no upstream file deleted).
- 2026-10-16 (branch gt4gs/live, task 036): new files pcsx2/GSStreamReplayer.{h,cpp} (GS stream CPU
  provider), pcsx2-gt4gs/ (gt4-gs.exe frontend, derived from pcsx2-gsrunner/Main.cpp, and the no-throw
  StreamTransport adapter), 3rdparty/gt4recomp-gs-stream/ (MIT protocol files from GT4Recomp, vendored by
  hash). Modified: pcsx2/VMManager.cpp (boot a prepared GS stream without BIOS or disc; select its CPU
  provider), pcsx2/GSDumpReplayer.cpp (a stream counts as a dump replay; serial from the stream; no dump
  overlay), common/Console.cpp (console text is also written to redirected standard handles),
  pcsx2/CMakeLists.txt, CMakeLists.txt and cmake/BuildParameters.cmake (sources, hash check, ENABLE_GT4GS),
  the dependency script (vswhere -products *), the packaging script and the gt4gs-windows workflow (build
  pcsx2-gt4gs).
- Later changes will be listed here with dates, in the same form.

GPLv3 section 5
---------------
Modified versions carry prominent notices stating that they were modified, and the date of the
modification (listed above). The notices in each file are otherwise kept.

Source
------
The corresponding source is the git tag of each release (gt4gs-v*) at
https://github.com/moesuito/gt4recomp-gs. Each GitHub Release attaches a source archive of that tag
(GPLv3 section 6(d)). SOURCE.txt in the zip names the exact commit.

GT4Recomp GS stream protocol (MIT)
----------------------------------
3rdparty/gt4recomp-gs-stream/ holds files from https://github.com/moesuito/gt4-staticrecomp
(native/gs_stream/, commit 57d1fa5) under the MIT license (3rdparty/gt4recomp-gs-stream/LICENSE.MIT).
pcsx2-gt4gs/StreamTransport.{h,cpp} are MIT as well. MIT code is compatible with GPL-3.0-or-later.

Bundled third-party components
------------------------------
The package contains the DLLs that the build links at runtime, copied from the dependency build
(build-dependencies-gt4gs.bat). The exact list is in SOURCE.txt of each zip. Their licenses (from the
upstream projects, pinned versions in the script) are:

- SDL3 (3.4.12): zlib license
- shaderc (2026.2), glslang, SPIRV-Headers, SPIRV-Tools: Apache-2.0 (with the LLVM exception where
  applicable) and the upstream licenses of those projects
- FFmpeg (8.1): the build uses --enable-gpl (for libx264) and libsvtav1, so the FFmpeg DLLs are
  under GPL-2.0-or-later as a whole. This is compatible with GPL-3.0-or-later distribution.
- x264 (static, in FFmpeg): GPL-2.0-or-later
- SVT-AV1 (4.0.1): BSD-3-Clause-Clear plus the AOMedia patent license
- Opus (1.6.1): BSD-3-Clause
- libvpl (2.16.0), AMF headers (1.5.0), nv-codec-headers (13.0.19.0): MIT
- zlib (1.3.2): zlib license
- libpng (1.6.58, APNG patch): libpng license
- libjpeg-turbo (3.2.0): BSD-3-Clause, IJG and zlib terms
- libwebp (1.6.0): BSD-3-Clause
- FreeType (2.14.3): FreeType License (FTL) or GPL-2.0-or-later
- HarfBuzz (14.2.0): MIT
- LZ4 (1.10.0): BSD-2-Clause
- Zstandard (1.5.7): BSD-3-Clause or GPL-2.0-or-later (dual)
- PlutoVG (1.3.2), PlutoSVG (0.0.7): MIT
- rapidyaml (0.12.1): MIT
- DirectX-Headers (1.619.1), Agility SDK (1.619.2): MIT (Microsoft)

The license texts of the upstream projects are in their source archives. This list is a
convenience summary, not legal advice; the license of each bundled file is the one of its project.

No game code, game data, BIOS, keys or disc images are part of this repository or of its releases.
